Now I understand the flow. The `unrounded` array is filled at the end of `TT_Vary_Apply_Glyph_Deltas` for all `n_points`. But there's a subtle issue: if `error` is set (goto Fail3) before the loop that fills `unrounded`, then `unrounded` is not filled. But then in `TT_Process_Simple_Glyph`, after the call, it checks `if ( error ) return error;` before using `unrounded`. So that's fine.

Wait, but there's a subtle issue. Let me re-read the code in `TT_Process_Simple_Glyph`:

```c
unrounded = gloader->current.extra_points2;
error = TT_Vary_Apply_Glyph_Deltas( ... );

/* recalculate linear horizontal and vertical advances */
if ( !( loader->face->variation_support & TT_FACE_FLAG_VAR_HADVANCE ) )
  loader->linear = FT_PIX_ROUND( unrounded[n_points - 3].x -
                                 unrounded[n_points - 4].x ) / 64;
if ( !( loader->face->variation_support & TT_FACE_FLAG_VAR_VADVANCE ) )
  loader->vadvance = FT_PIX_ROUND( unrounded[n_points - 1].x -
                                   unrounded[n_points - 2].x ) / 64;

if ( error )
  return error;
```

So `unrounded[n_points-3]`, `unrounded[n_points-4]`, `unrounded[n_points-1]`, `unrounded[n_points-2]` are read BEFORE checking `error`. If `TT_Vary_Apply_Glyph_Deltas` returns an error (goto Fail3 before filling unrounded), then these reads use uninitialized values!

But wait, in the current code, the `if ( error ) return error;` is AFTER the reads. Let me check the fix. The fix likely moved the `if ( error ) return error;` check before the reads of `unrounded`.

Let me look at the actual fix commit. Let me search the freetype2 git history. The fix was in commit around May 13, 2019. Let me look at the actual freetype2 commit.

Let me check the ChangeLog for the fix.

